re uxoris)"],"extract":"Alfonso IX (15 August 1171 – 23 or 24 September 1230) was King of León from the death of his father Ferdinand II in 1188 until his own death.\nHe took steps towards modernizing and democratizing his dominion and founded the University of Salamanca in 1218. In 1188 he summoned the first parliament reflecting the fullest representation of the citizenry ever seen in Western Europe, the Cortes of León.\nAlfonso took part in the Reconquista, conquering several territories within Extremadura, capturing Mérida and Badajoz in 1230, which allowed for the eventual conquest of Seville during the reign of his son Ferdinand III. He was also involved in numerous conflicts with Pope Celestine III, being interdicted on account of the nature of his marriages.","wp_description":"King of León and Galicia from 1188 to 1230","wikipedia_url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alfonso_IX_of_Le%C3%B3n","image_lead":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1c/Adeffonsus%2C_king_of_Galicia_and_Leon_%28detail%29.jpg","thumbnail":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1c/Adeffonsus%2C_king_of_Galicia_and_Leon_%28detail%29.jpg","chat_ready":true,"display_from":1188,"display_to":1230}